# A lap is SNE (skipping the exit), SUB, JMP back: the SUBs are instructions 2, 5 and 8, so x (B of
# cell 6) is 1 after 7 and 0 after 8; then JMP back (9), SNE does not skip (10), JMP leaves (11) and
# MOV marks done (A of cell 6) at 12. A loop that never left would never mark it.
golden: bbctests/examples/while_ne.bbc
cell 7 6 DAT.F #0, #1
cell 8 6 DAT.F #0, #0
cell 11 6 DAT.F #0, #0
cell 12 6 DAT.F #1, #0
cell 50 6 DAT.F #1, #0
alive 100
